    "notes": [
      {
        "moduleIds": [
          1
        ],
        "content": "## Prepare payroll from Gusto time data with Claude and approve in Slack\n\nSmall HR and finance teams that run payroll checks by hand every period and still find errors after the fact.\n\n### How it works\nTrigger: Runs on the cut-off date each period, plus a preview run three days earlier so managers can fix missing approvals.\n1. Collect period inputs\n2. Normalise into one employee ledger\n3. Validate against policy\n4. Anomaly review\n5. Send the exceptions report\n6. Wait for approval\n7. Push the run to the provider\n8. Reconcile after the run\nEvery AI step is followed by a \"Needs a person?\" gate that parks low-confidence items; the write-back waits for an approval.\n\n### Setup\n1. Open \"Config (edit me)\" and fill in the fields (names, approver, quiet hours, thresholds).\n2. Add credentials: Anthropic, plus Gusto / ADP / Rippling / Deel, Slack, Google Sheets.\n3. Run once with test_mode on, read the output, then switch the trigger on.\n\n### Customization tips\nSet the pay-period rules and the anomaly thresholds in the Config node; connect Gusto, ADP, Rippling or Deel.\nGuardrail to keep: The workflow never submits without an explicit human approval; the Wait node is the control.\n\nFull blueprint: https://agentmelt.com/workflows/payroll-automation/",
        "isFilterNote": false,
        "metadata": {
          "color": "#F5D451"
        }
      }
    ],
    "zone": "eu1.make.com"
  }
